"><li>What type of military force/guardsmen does the Thundering Falls tribe have if any?</li> <li>What would happen to be the required or recommended reading for me to be up to speed for this game?</li> </ol><br /> I'll try to have the character done and waiting for when we can actually get started. Let's hope that we can get more to join in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T14:27:01-07:00","id":139799,"title":"","content":"The only thing you should consider &quot;required&quot; reading is the Masters book. As long as you are familiar with the Autochthonia's aesthetic of &quot;gigantic factory world&quot;, there's not much about the Octet that bears heavily on the Taken. The section from MoEP:Alchemicals on spirits and the rules for Gremlin Syndrome might prove useful to you. Autochthonia's a lot of fun as a setting, though, so I doubt you'd be bored by any of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T18:25:48-07:00","id":144002,"title":"","content":"Yep, I already read the Masters book back around Thanksgiving (American) and I will probably cover the pertinent sections again. I will also look into the recommended areas of MoEP: Alchemicals if not the whole thing.<br /> <br /> A Few Questions: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>For the Favored Abilities, Domini aren't restricted like Heroic Mortals, right? They can have skills that aren't favored higher than the favored ones?</li> <li>Also experience expenditures for Attributes and Abilities are the same as listed at the end of the Storytelling Chapter of Ex2 Core.</li> <li>For mechanical purposes it doesn't really matter what type of elemental is trapped in the Binding Stone, but what would be the most likely metal elemental that could get trapped, as I am thinking of an Ironsoul?</li> <li>All the backgrounds mentioned in the Character Creation section of Masters are fair game. Would you recommend some more than others?</li> </ol><br /> I'm sure I will come up with more questions as time goes on. Please bear with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T10:26:56-07:00","id":144592,"title":"","content":"1. You can certainly have other Abilities be higher than your Favored Abilities, if I'm remembering my rules correctly. If that's not in there, I should have put it there.<br /> 2. Yes.<br /> 3. There's some gorilla-like metal elementals in MoEP:Alchemicals that guard metal conduits that come across as fairly common. I forget the name. If those don't work for you, feel free to make something up.<br /> 4. Nothing stands out as particularly important. Savant is a rare background for the Taken, and you probably won't see legion-sized Commands.<br /> <br /> I also seem to have forgotten to answer your question about the military forces of the tribe. My conception of the tribes is that they all have either a militia-type arrangement or some form of standing military in order to defend themselves against the dangers of other tribes, elementals, the Extermination's raids, and so on. How developed this is depends on the story. I'd say that right now the Thundering Falls tribe is running at an all time high on proportional military service.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T06:24:24-07:00","id":146625,"title":"","content":"I have an Ironsoul ready to go. He is a member of whatever police/tribal guard force the tribe has. He became one of the Domini so he could do that job more effectively.<br /> <br /> The Gezlak does appear to be a good fit for the backstory on the binding stone as that elemental has a similar motivation to the character. So, the only real questions I have at this point mostly involve backgrounds. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I have the Mentor background at 2. I was hoping for a veteran tribal guard to be the mentor, but I will be willing to work something else out.</li> <li>I have a trophy stone at 2. I would like it to be a Crystal type, but I am not sure what extra abilities it would grant and I don't have an artifact to have it resonate with yet.</li> <li>Speaking of equipment, as I have no Resources dots I would guess any equipment would be borrowed from the guards/police force and leave it to your discretion what I actually have.</li> <li>It is a little confusing what is actually rolled when I attempt to use (Element) Bolt Attack. It mentions that (Aspect) is used instead of an ability, but it makes no mention of what stat is used with the roll. In addition the attack as listed with accuracy +(Aspect), which would suggest it would be treated as a ranged weapon that would use a normal Attribute (Dexterity?) + Ability roll with a bonus to said roll equal to (Aspect). I'm going to assume you wanted Dexterity + (Aspect) to be the roll for the attack. This seems to make it less effective than a mundane bow in that the bow would use Dexterity + Archery + Accuracy from the bow itself (Longbow only). I imagine the idea would be to make it weaker than the Dragon-Blooded Elemental Bolt Attack charm, but that seems to only work if you consider that the Dragon-Bloods can pour essence into it to make it deal more damage. The fact that they can use an ability for the roll as opposed to an aspect stat is only more efficient if you consider exp. cost differences.</li> </ol><br /> I'm sure I will think of other stuff later. Also, would we like to create an OOC thread in the Play by Post subforum so I can post the character there or would you rather I post it somewhere else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T15:19:54-07:00","id":147202,"title":"","content":"1. A veteran guard is certainly possible. What do you want out of him as a character?<br /> 2. If you want some quick and easy stuff, look over 2 dot hearthstones. If you want to make something up, just run it by me. The lack of an artifact is a tricky spot. How tightly spread is your background dots?<br /> 3. I find your poverty strange, but then I haven't read your backstory yet.<br /> 4. That one has come up a few times and I blame myself for being unclear. Attacks are almost always made with Dexterity, so I didn't think to mention it. The weapon stat line, though, has the accuracy as +Essence, not +Aspect. So an attack with (Aspect) Bolt Attack would be Dexterity + Aspect + Essence. When comparing (Aspect) Bolt Attack to (Elemental) Bolt Attack, Stonebearers do seem to have the better Charm. This is because of a combination of factors - the basics of the Stonebearer version is pulled from a God-Blooded mutation in Scroll of Heroes, Domini have smaller Essence pools (they start at 11ish) than Dragon-Blooded and so are paying a lot proportionally to use the Charm, and the Charm hasn't really been playtested yet.<br /> <br /> I'd say just post the character sheet here for now. Maybe staying at the top of the forum will get this game a bit more exposure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T21:52:21-07:00","id":147572,"title":"","content":"1. For the Mentor dots I would like to just have a guy that would give me advice for commanding my squad of guards and maybe some pointers on the more political aspects of things as the character seems to be new to this stuff.<br /> 2. Background dots are not overly tight. I really actually had trouble spending them all. I reasoned that I could gain an artifact during play without too much trouble, but switching around a dot to just get a Hearthstone Amulet wouldn't hurt.<br /> 3. The character is pretty much &quot;All-In&quot; with the guards. He dedicated himself more fully to the &quot;family business&quot; both after becoming a Dominus and after the death of his brother (where the Crystal Aspect stone comes from)<br /> 4. Thanks for clearing that one up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-na