px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Experience Gained: </b>0<br /> <b>Experience Spent: </b>0<br /> <b>Experience Left: </b>0</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b><u>History</u></b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Alekzandir was born to a Thundering Falls Tribe family whose only profession was that of guardian to the tribe. He joined the guards as soon as he was old enough. He eagerly accepted the challenge of becoming a Dominus as soon as a new stone was available for bidding. He succeeded in gaining control over the raging Gezlak elemental inside the stone. He was thankful that he had a skilled surgeon for the implantation because there was little harm done implanting the stone, giving him a wider margin for error before failure became lethal.<br /> <br /> When a routine patrol with his elder brother, Yuri turned into an incursion by gremlins the brothers found themselves in a fight for their lives. Yuri was an experienced Glassknife with a storied binding stone and he took the brunt of the attack on himself. Alekzandir barely survived, only then by being able to will his wounds closed when he was left for dead. Yuri was not so lucky. Alek returned to the tribe with his brother's binding stone in hand.<br /> <br /> Since the death of Yuri, Alek has become even more involved with the Guards to the point that he has been given a command. He uses much of the payments he earns from being a guard to take care of Yuri's widow and children.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":1146,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","user":"Belkra","date":".  Added Combat Information, attunement modifiers to Essence Pool, and final update to specialties. 05-30-2014, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T15:43:12-07:00","id":153198,"title":"","content":"Alright.<br /> <br /> I like the backstory for the most part. The only bit out of place is the bit about the surgeon - the surgeon has no direct influence over a Dominus' chance of success in mastering an elemental. Also, 8+ Willpower is certainly common in char-op, but your character's willpower is exceptionally high from an IC stand point.<br /> <br /> Mechanics-wise, I have some concerns.<br /> <br /> First, are you aware that you can probably get the same Ability list as you have for 3 bonus points cheaper? Use freebie dots for Investigation, Survival, and Thrown and then buy your Resistance or Integrity dots with bonus points for half the price.<br /> <br /> Second, you could change your Specialty in Inspiring Troops to Inspiring Others if you wanted and you probably should change Countering Stealth to something a little more specific, like Ambushes.<br /> <br /> Third, are you sure you only want Dexterity 2? It's sort of the god-stat of combat. I can see why you have Stamina 4, but you could probably drop a dot of Strength without feeling it too much.<br /> <br /> Fourth, are you sure you want both Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, and Appearance 1? Charisma and Manipulation are hard to leverage at the same time and Appearance is pretty key in social MDV values.<br /> <br /> Fifth, are you sure you want to use a Focus Talent purchase on Resisting Poison? It's one of the only ways to increase your Excellency cap (right now, you can buy 1 die) and you only get three of them per Excellency. I can certainly see resisting poison as useful, especially given the local environment, but I feel I should double check that you've considered the ramifications.<br /> <br /> Sixth, I think you could do with Resources 1 as you are not literally penniless and you would have great use for a jade hearthstone amulet or artifact weapon<br /> <br /> Seventh, I think you should change your Intimacy from Great Maker to Machine King (the Taken's term for him) and should drop the Intimacies to the Divine Ministers and to the Octet. While I mentioned them heavily, I don't think that the Taken are aware of the Divine Ministers or the Octet as such. The Taken, as far as my conception of them goes, are aware that the Machine King has his faithful mortal servants (they term them &quot;slaves&quot;) but are not aware of what their current organization is. They also probably have lumped the Divine Ministers in with the rest of the exmachina as the spawn of the Machine King.<br /> <br /> On the whole, I think you are looking pretty solid. I don't think I'll have much trouble motivating your character with the plot I have in mind. Don't feel you have to change everything I pointed out - most of it is just me making sure you are aware of the mechanical ramifications of your choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:05:34-07:00","id":153335,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback! You've helped me keep the character concept I had in mind and allowed me some things that make for an easier time of things and afford more optimization. Let's address these concerns in order. (You should be able to see the changes reflected in the sheet.)<br /> <br /> First, I made the corrections you suggested and freed up the bonus points for other things. It would make sense that the character would gain the Integrity points after becoming a Dominus and therefore use bonus points for them.<br /> <br /> Second, I changed the specialties. The one for Presence is as you suggested, but the one for Awareness is a little more tricky. Essentially I want the guy to have a bonus to awareness when he is doing what he does best, standing guard or patrolling. If that has to be two different specialty purchases I will go with one and free up a bonus point to get the other.<br /> <br /> Third, the low Dexterity score was something I decided I wanted to start. It gives the character room to grow and I am not necessarily worried that much about optimization as I am about telling a good story. If the character is memorable because his Dexterity is crappy, I consider that a good thing.<br /> <br /> Fourth, this is pretty much the same as the last point. I want him to be rough around the edges, at least at the start of things.<br /> <br /> Fifth, I realize that I could probably spend this specialty on my Metal Bolt Attack charm, but I think I will leave it as is because of concept reasons.<br /> <br /> Sixth, thanks to bonus point optimizations this is done. Two in Resources and one in Artifact so I can actually make use of the Trophy Stone.<br /> <br /> Seventh, the intimacies are fixed. Admittedly I was having trouble finding things to put in this category, but after thinking about it a little more there are no problems.<br /> <br /> The only thing that is needed now is equipment. I understand that the rule from Core is that I can have a small number of items to start and none of these items may cost more than my Resources background. So, a breastplate is a go, but super heavy plate is right out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath